 misguided view this  is very short range because  what many of these ideas kind of are  premised on is that these vaccines are  just there for the taking  that they don't require effort that they  don't require mental  uh mental concentration mental uh these  are products of people's minds that they  just don't  appear and if we remove those incentives  if we remove the ability of  companies to invest and plan and think  about what how they can offset those  risks because they think they're going  to get revenue because of the patent  protection  who's going to want to innovate in this  field anymore who's going to want to  enter into these agreements during  pandemics  if at the end this can be just taken  away from them  so i think that's that what they're not  seeing they're not seeing this long  range and  and and i think that's what we have to  to really combat because if we lose  the ability to innovate and have the  biopharmaceutical companies  develop products that all our lives  depend on we're all going to be worse  off i think we can solve covet 19  without  violating intellectual property rights  that was a mesh adulterer from the johns  hopkins  university center for health security
 

